# PHASE ORCHESTRATION V1.2.1

> **Purpose**: Manage the lean 3-phase WSR composition workflow. The LLM infers maximum context silently in Phase 0 (no script invocation), asks the user a single batch in Phase 1, drafts and validates in Phase 2 — total 2 stop points, 4-file output bundle.
>
> **Goal**: Composing a WSR via this agent should be FASTER than typing the email manually.
>
> **v1.2.1 change — stateless design**: the WSR flow completes in a single chat session; the LLM's context window holds the entire run (reference + Phase 0 inferences + Phase 1 batch reply + Phase 2 draft). No runtime state file (`.wsr-state.json`) is written or required. `run_metadata.json` is still produced at SP2 as a *post-hoc audit artifact* (not runtime state).
>
> **Enforcement**: See `@03_Mandatory_Stop_Points.mdc`

