## PHASE 1 — Per-Section Updates (SINGLE BATCH — Stop #1)

**Purpose:** Present the inferred draft + ask the user a SINGLE batch of updates. The user replies once with everything.

**Tasks:**
1. Render the 6 inferred sections (Mode A) OR placeholder skeletons (Mode B)
2. Add the leaves prompt
3. Add the Jira-paste prompt for metrics (LLM will parse the reply natively in Phase 2)
4. Add a free-form "any other updates" line
5. **Bidirectional sycophancy guard preview** — if inferred status is Green AND inferred Attention/blockers list is non-empty, OR vice versa, include a one-line nudge in the batch
6. Mark inferred fields with `[from reference]` so the user knows what's already known
7. Mark missing fields with `⚠️ MISSING — please provide`

### RGV (Read-Generate-Verify)
```
1. READ:    Phase 0 inferences from context → Expected: 6 sections + status + metrics + sender + region
2. GENERATE: Single batch message with all inferences shown + 4 prompts
3. VERIFY:   Every required field is either [from reference] OR ⚠️ MISSING in the batch
4. FIX:      Any inference key missing from batch → fix before presenting
```

### Stop Point #1 — Single Batch Format
```
🧞‍♂️ WSR DRAFT — please review and reply ONCE with all updates

📇 Project Card  (auto-filled — date is today)
   Project : {name} [from reference]
   Region  : {region} [from reference]
   Date    : {today auto}
   Sender  : {sender} [from reference]
   CC      : {cc list} [from reference]

🚦 Status — Overall Delivery: {color} [from reference]   GDC Project: {color} [from reference]
{optional: ⚠️ Sycophancy nudge — "Reference says Green; you may want to reconsider if {reason}"}

📝 Section drafts (from reference):

  Summary of WSR:
  {bullet block}

  Completed:        {bullet block}
  In Progress:      {bullet block}

  Ask :             {None as of now | items}
  Attention:        {items}

📊 Metrics — please paste your Jira sprint export OR describe this week's metrics
   (capacity actual/planned, planned vs delivered stories, defects per phase)
   → {paste here}

📅 Days — leaves/holidays this week?
   Format: Name=days_off (e.g., Akshay=2, Bhawna=1) or "none"
   → {your input}

✏️ Any other updates / additions / removals to any section?
   → {your input or "none"}

Reply with everything in one message.
```

**STOP. Wait for the user's single batch reply.**

